# Frontend integration

- Call only `VITE_API_URL` (gateway). Never fetch microservices directly.
- Staff backoffice is **path routing** under `/admin/*` in this same app (same port). Do not add a second Vite port for admin.
- Quote/contact submit must persist via `POST /v1/quotes` or `POST /v1/contact` once those routes exist. WhatsApp is a follow-up channel, not storage.
- Keep bilingual routes and prerender. Fleet/CMS data will replace hardcoded arrays without changing URL slugs.
- Playwright SSG must not require API auth or a live gateway: use the bundled fleet seed at build (`__VIPCAR_PRERENDER__`); prefer live catalog at runtime.
- Indicative TND prices are display-only until a confirmed quote is returned.
- Keep analytics events: `quote_submit`, `service_selected`, `phone_click`, `whatsapp_click`, `email_click`.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — message is the only record
location.href = `${WA}?text=${encodeURIComponent(msg)}`;

// ✅ GOOD — persist, then optionally notify
await fetch(`${apiUrl}/v1/quotes`, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(payload) });
```
